bug_report:
unspecified VLA bound formatted as [0] instead of [*] in -Wvla-parameter
The format of the array (VLA) in the note and warning below isn't quite right: it should match the bound used in the source but instead uses the [0] notation because [*] and [0] are internally represented the same.

$ cat a.c && gcc -S -Wall a.c
f (int,   int[1][*]);
void f (int n, int[1][n]);

void g (int n, int[1][n]);
void g (int,   int[1][*]);

a.c:2:16: warning: argument 2 of type ‘int[1][n]’ declared as a variable length array [-Wvla-parameter]
    2 | void f (int n, int[1][n]);
      |                ^~~~~~~~~
a.c:1:16: note: previously declared as an ordinary array ‘int[1][0]’
    1 | void f (int,   int[1][*]);
      |                ^~~~~~~~~
a.c:5:16: warning: argument 2 of type ‘int[1][0]’ declared as an ordinary array [-Wvla-parameter]
    5 | void g (int,   int[1][*]);
      |                ^~~~~~~~~
a.c:4:16: note: previously declared as a variable length array ‘int[1][n]’
    4 | void g (int n, int[1][n]);
      |                ^~~~~~~~~
